# Cache-Aware and Cache-Oblivious Sorting

## Requirements
- GCC 10+ on Linux x86-64
- POSIX environment (uses posix_memalign, madvise)

## Build
g++ -O3 -march=native -flto -funroll-loops -o sort_bench sort.cpp

## Run
./sort_bench 10000000    # pass N as argument, default is 10M

## Output
Prints average time in ms for Cache-Aware, Cache-Oblivious, and std::sort.
Correctness is verified against std::sort reference output.

## Plots
- `line_chart.png`: Shows performance scaling (time in ms vs. input size N) across all three sorting algorithms for a fully random distribution.
- `Performance_Comparison.png`: A bar chart comparing the execution times of the algorithms at N=10M across both the random and nearly-sorted distributions.